===Etymology 1===
{{root|pt|ine-pro|*h₁eḱ-|*ǵʰwer-}}
{{dercat|pt|itc-pro|inh=1}}
From {{m|pt|zebro}}, from {{inh|pt|roa-opt|zebro}}, {{m|roa-opt|ezebro||European wild ass}}, from {{inh|pt|VL.|*eciferus}}, from {{inh|pt|la|equiferus||wild horse}}, from {{m|la|equus||horse}} + {{m|la|ferus||wild}}. Compare {{cog|es|cebra}}.

Senses 2 and 3 of the word comes from the popular Brazilian [[betting]] game {{m|pt|jogo do bicho}}, in which the animal is absent, therefore it is unlikely that a zebra will be drawn.

